# Build-time tooling vulnerabilities inherited from the python:3.11-slim base
# image (setuptools' vendored copies of jaraco.context / wheel). These packages
# are NOT used in the runtime execution path — the container only runs uvicorn —
# and the Dockerfile already upgrades pip/setuptools/wheel. These entries cover
# any vendored residue trivy still reports. Revisit when the base image ships
# patched vendored versions.
CVE-2026-23949
CVE-2026-24049

# msgpack and setuptools both come from pip's own internal build-provenance
# SBOM (usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pip/_vendor/bom.cdx.json),
# which Trivy ingests directly (see its own "Third-party SBOM may lead to
# inaccurate vulnerability detection" warning). That SBOM documents pip's
# vendored msgpack (used internally by pip's HTTP cache) and a historical
# setuptools version from pip's own build — neither is the setuptools our
# Dockerfile actually installs, and neither is imported by our code.
# Confirmed the current latest pip release (26.2.1) still ships this SBOM
# verbatim, so there is no newer pip to upgrade to. Revisit once upstream pip
# publishes an updated bom.cdx.json.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
